# Copy to apps/mobile/.env and fill values from the shared Supabase project
# (same project as sibling Edubite / web — map NEXT_PUBLIC_* → EXPO_PUBLIC_*).
#
# NEVER put SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY, Google Client Secret, or DB passwords here.
# Mobile may only use: project URL + anon/publishable key (+ optional public client IDs).

EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://bytsiknhtcnlxwzgqkrd.supabase.co
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# --- Manual dashboard checklist (Google OAuth via Supabase) ---
# 1) Google Cloud → Credentials → Web client (keep existing web login):
#    Authorized redirect URI (MUST stay Supabase, not the app scheme):
#      https://bytsiknhtcnlxwzgqkrd.supabase.co/auth/v1/callback
# 2) Optional native clients (recommended for production):
#    - Android: package com.edubite.app + SHA-1 / SHA-256 of your keystore
#    - iOS: bundle ID com.edubite.app
# 3) Supabase → Authentication → Providers → Google:
#    - Enable Google
#    - Client IDs order: Web client ID first, then iOS, then Android (comma-separated if multi)
#    - Client secret: Web client secret only (server-side in Supabase — never in the app)
#    - Leave “Skip nonce checks” DISABLED (this app uses browser PKCE, not native ID-token)
# 4) Supabase → Authentication → URL Configuration → Redirect URLs, add:
#      edubite://auth/callback
#    For Expo Go also add the exact makeRedirectUri() value logged as [auth] starting Google OAuth
#      (often exp://127.0.0.1:8081/--/auth/callback or similar)
# 5) Site URL can remain the web app origin; mobile uses Additional Redirect URLs above.
